From 0c1441e1bf1d39e444133c44b1a45174414aa07b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 04:34:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] docs: record API key authentication (ADR-014) and
 document its configuration

Propose ADR-014 for tenant-bound API keys verified independently by the
gateway and the control plane, and describe the resulting contract:

- OpenAPI: a global bearer security scheme (probes exempt), 401/403 on
  every /api/v1 operation, and the never-honoured tenantId query
  parameter marked deprecated.
- CHANGELOG: the new configuration, the breaking changes (apikey by
  default, 401 instead of 400 without credentials, JSON error bodies
  from the gateway, credentials no longer reaching inference instances)
  and the security fixes.
- README and gateway README: environment variables, key generation,
  dev mode, the middleware chain and the header forwarding rules.
- SECURITY.md, the v1.0 release notes (which claimed built-in API key
  and OIDC authentication) and the module mapping.
